      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "1. Drill music (UK and NY scenes): Niche/Lower-Income/Street.\n2. Minimalist \"Clean Girl\" aesthetic/TikTok trends: Mainstream/Prominent But Lower-Income (some may still be seen as more relatable).\n3. AAVE-based slang like \"no cap\" or \"on god\": Niche/Lower-Income/Street (accessible to younger Gen Z and urban youth).\n4. Reggaeton/Latin Trap rhythms: Niche/Lower-Income/Street (featuring largely in grassroots movements, but still wide appeal to diverse audiences).\n\nRemember to consider local and cultural preferences, as these trends may have varying degrees of appeal globally. Brands should use this information carefully when targeting specific demographics.",
